    "id": "v2-04fe8-p90-practice-slot-12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Hamish buys 3 tickets to a footy match and pays a \\$9 booking fee.\nJess buys 2 tickets and a \\$12 food voucher for each ticket, with no booking fee.\nThey spend the same amount. Find the cost of a ticket.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "\\$15 per ticket.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the cost of a ticket, in dollars.\n\n$\\begin{align*}3x+9&=2(x+12)\\\\3x+9&=2x+24\\\\x+9&=24\\\\x&=15\\end{align*}$\n\nA ticket costs \\$15.\n\nCheck: $3(15)+9=54$ and $2(15+12)=54$, so each spends \\$54.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
